<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kalaburagi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Gulbarga, Ahsanabad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gulbarga, officially Kalaburagi since 2014, is a city in northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ala-ud-din-bahman-shah">Alauddin Hasan Bahman Shah</a> made it the first capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bahmani-sultanate">Bahmani Sultanate</a> in 1347, and it remained the capital until the court moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bidar">Bidar</a> in the 1420s. The Bahmani fort with its great domed mosque, the royal tombs and the shrine of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesu-daraz">Gesu Daraz</a> date from that period.</p></div>
